      "title": "Make the XML DTDs more spec compliant",
      "message": "Make the XML DTDs more spec compliant\n\nProcessing Instructions in XML are defined such that the PITarget must\nfollow immediately after the initial '<?', i.e. there can be no\nwhitespace. The PITarget is a Name, which cannot have \":\" as a character\nother than the initial character.\n\n  https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#NT-PI\n  https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#NT-Name\n\nIf we later want to parse the DTDs with a compliant XML and DTD parser\ninstead of a hand-rolled flex and lemon based parser, they should be\nmade more compliant. Change the DTDs and the Lemon parser accordingly.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
